{"ID":74,"post_author":"1","post_date":"2026-03-05 17:34:30","post_date_gmt":"2026-03-05 17:34:30","post_content":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Kanchi Kamakoti Upa Peetham - History & Acharya Lineage<\/title>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n    <style>\n        \/* Language Toggle Button Basic Styles *\/\n        .language-toggle {\n            text-align: right;\n            padding: 15px 20px 0;\n            background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #fff5e6, #fffaf5);\n        }\n        #lang-btn {\n            background-color: #d9531e;\n            color: white;\n            border: none;\n            padding: 8px 20px;\n            font-size: 1em;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            border-radius: 20px;\n            cursor: pointer;\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(217, 83, 30, 0.3);\n            transition: background-color 0.3s ease;\n        }\n        #lang-btn:hover { background-color: #b34700; }\n    <\/style>\n<\/head>\n<body>\n        <!-- Language Toggle Button -->\n            <button id=\"lang-btn\" onclick=\"toggleLanguage()\">Switch to Hindi (\u0939\u093f\u0902\u0926\u0940)<\/button>\n        <!-- Header Banner Section -->\n        <header>\n            <h2>Kanchi Kamakoti Upa Peetham<\/h2>\n            <h2 style=\"display: none;\">\u0915\u093e\u0902\u091a\u0940 \u0915\u093e\u092e\u0915\u094b\u091f\u093f \u0909\u092a \u092a\u0940\u0920<\/h2>\n            <h1>History & Acharya Lineage<\/h1>\n            <h1 style=\"display: none;\">\u092a\u0940\u0920 \u0915\u093e \u0907\u0924\u093f\u0939\u093e\u0938 \u090f\u0935\u0902 \u0906\u091a\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f \u092a\u0930\u0902\u092a\u0930\u093e<\/h1>\n            <p>The Glorious History and Unbroken Lineage of Kanchi Kamakoti Upa Peetham<\/p>\n            <p style=\"display: none;\">\u0915\u093e\u0902\u091a\u0940 \u0915\u093e\u092e\u0915\u094b\u091f\u093f \u0909\u092a \u092a\u0940\u0920 \u0915\u093e \u0917\u094c\u0930\u0935\u0936\u093e\u0932\u0940 \u0907\u0924\u093f\u0939\u093e\u0938 \u0914\u0930 \u0905\u0916\u0902\u0921 \u0906\u091a\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f \u092a\u0930\u0902\u092a\u0930\u093e<\/p>\n        <\/header>\n        <!-- Main Content Area -->\n        <main>\n            <!-- Introduction & Present Acharya Section -->\n            <section>\n                <!-- Present Acharya Image -->\n                    <img src=\"https:\/\/shivbodhtrust.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/kanchi-Sri-Satya-Chandrashekarendra-Saraswathi-Shankaracharya-swami-peetha.jpg\" alt=\"Sri Satya Chandrashekarendra Saraswathi Aacharya\">\n                    The Revered 71st Aacharya\n                    \u092a\u0930\u092e \u092a\u0942\u091c\u094d\u092f 71\u0935\u0947\u0902 \u0906\u091a\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f\n                <!-- History Text -->\n                    <h2>History of Establishment and Present State<\/h2>\n                    <h2 style=\"display: none;\">\u0938\u094d\u0925\u093e\u092a\u0928\u093e \u0915\u093e \u0907\u0924\u093f\u0939\u093e\u0938 \u0914\u0930 \u0935\u0930\u094d\u0924\u092e\u093e\u0928 \u0938\u094d\u0935\u0930\u0942\u092a<\/h2>\n                        <p>The Kanchi Kamakoti Upa Peetham is located in the sacred and ancient city of Kanchipuram, Tamil Nadu, India. For centuries, this Upa Peetham has been a revered center for the preservation of Vedic knowledge, Sanatana Dharma, and social welfare. Its main objective has been the protection of the Vedas, cow protection (Go-Seva), and the propagation of spiritual wisdom. This sacred Upa Peetham boasts an <strong>unbroken and glorious lineage of 71 Aacharyas<\/strong>, who have completely dedicated their lives to public welfare.<\/p>\n                        <p style=\"display: none;\">\u0915\u093e\u0902\u091a\u0940 \u0915\u093e\u092e\u0915\u094b\u091f\u093f \u0909\u092a \u092a\u0940\u0920 \u092d\u093e\u0930\u0924 \u0915\u0947 \u0924\u092e\u093f\u0932\u0928\u093e\u0921\u0941 \u0930\u093e\u091c\u094d\u092f \u0915\u0947 \u092a\u0935\u093f\u0924\u094d\u0930 \u0914\u0930 \u092a\u094d\u0930\u093e\u091a\u0940\u0928 \u0928\u0917\u0930 \u0915\u093e\u0902\u091a\u0940\u092a\u0941\u0930\u092e \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0938\u094d\u0925\u093f\u0924 \u0939\u0948\u0964 \u0938\u0926\u093f\u092f\u094b\u0902 \u0938\u0947 \u092f\u0939 \u0909\u092a \u092a\u0940\u0920 \u0935\u0948\u0926\u093f\u0915 \u091c\u094d\u091e\u093e\u0928, \u0938\u0928\u093e\u0924\u0928 \u0927\u0930\u094d\u092e \u0915\u0947 \u0938\u0902\u0930\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0923 \u0914\u0930 \u0938\u092e\u093e\u091c \u0915\u0932\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0923 \u0915\u093e \u090f\u0915 \u0935\u0902\u0926\u0928\u0940\u092f \u0915\u0947\u0902\u0926\u094d\u0930 \u0930\u0939\u093e \u0939\u0948\u0964 \u0907\u0938 \u0909\u092a \u092a\u0940\u0920 \u0915\u0940 \u0938\u094d\u0925\u093e\u092a\u0928\u093e \u0915\u093e \u092e\u0941\u0916\u094d\u092f \u0909\u0926\u094d\u0926\u0947\u0936\u094d\u092f \u0935\u0947\u0926\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u0940 \u0930\u0915\u094d\u0937\u093e, \u0917\u094b-\u0938\u0947\u0935\u093e \u0914\u0930 \u0906\u0927\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0924\u094d\u092e\u093f\u0915 \u091c\u094d\u091e\u093e\u0928 \u0915\u093e \u092a\u094d\u0930\u091a\u093e\u0930-\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0938\u093e\u0930 \u0915\u0930\u0928\u093e \u0930\u0939\u093e \u0939\u0948\u0964 \u0907\u0938 \u092a\u0935\u093f\u0924\u094d\u0930 \u0909\u092a \u092a\u0940\u0920 \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0905\u092c \u0924\u0915 <strong>71 \u0906\u091a\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0902 \u0915\u0940 \u090f\u0915 \u0905\u0916\u0902\u0921 \u0914\u0930 \u0917\u094c\u0930\u0935\u0936\u093e\u0932\u0940 \u092a\u0930\u0902\u092a\u0930\u093e<\/strong> \u0930\u0939\u0940 \u0939\u0948, \u091c\u093f\u0928\u094d\u0939\u094b\u0902\u0928\u0947 \u0905\u092a\u0928\u093e \u0938\u0902\u092a\u0942\u0930\u094d\u0923 \u091c\u0940\u0935\u0928 \u091c\u0928-\u0915\u0932\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0923 \u0915\u0947 \u0932\u093f\u090f \u092a\u0942\u0930\u094d\u0923\u0924\u0903 \u0938\u092e\u0930\u094d\u092a\u093f\u0924 \u0915\u093f\u092f\u093e \u0939\u0948\u0964<\/p>\n                        <h3>Profound Reverence Among Devotees<\/h3>\n                        <h3 style=\"display: none;\">\u091c\u0928\u092e\u093e\u0928\u0938 \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0905\u0917\u093e\u0927 \u0936\u094d\u0930\u0926\u094d\u0927\u093e (Reverence among Devotees)<\/h3>\n                        <p>The entire life of the current 71st Aacharya, <strong>Sri Satya Chandrashekarendra Saraswathi<\/strong>, is dedicated to Sanatana Dharma. There is profound reverence for him among devotees across South India and the whole of Bharat. Due to his immense spiritual power and boundless dedication to Dharma, devotees consider him a <strong>great scholar and ascetic equivalent to a Shankaracharya<\/strong>, and worship him with the same deep devotion.<\/p>\n                        <p style=\"display: none;\">\u0935\u0930\u094d\u0924\u092e\u093e\u0928 71\u0935\u0947\u0902 \u0906\u091a\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f <strong>\u0936\u094d\u0930\u0940 \u0938\u0924\u094d\u092f \u091a\u0902\u0926\u094d\u0930\u0936\u0947\u0916\u0930\u0947\u0902\u0926\u094d\u0930 \u0938\u0930\u0938\u094d\u0935\u0924\u0940 \u091c\u0940<\/strong> \u0915\u093e \u0938\u0902\u092a\u0942\u0930\u094d\u0923 \u091c\u0940\u0935\u0928 \u0938\u0928\u093e\u0924\u0928 \u0927\u0930\u094d\u092e \u0915\u0947 \u0932\u093f\u090f \u0938\u092e\u0930\u094d\u092a\u093f\u0924 \u0939\u0948\u0964 \u0926\u0915\u094d\u0937\u093f\u0923 \u092d\u093e\u0930\u0924 \u0938\u0939\u093f\u0924 \u0938\u0902\u092a\u0942\u0930\u094d\u0923 \u092d\u093e\u0930\u0924\u0935\u0930\u094d\u0937 \u092e\u0947\u0902 \u0936\u094d\u0930\u0926\u094d\u0927\u093e\u0932\u0941\u0913\u0902 \u0915\u0947 \u092c\u0940\u091a \u0906\u091a\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f \u091c\u0940 \u0915\u0947 \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0924\u093f \u0905\u0917\u093e\u0927 \u0936\u094d\u0930\u0926\u094d\u0927\u093e \u0939\u0948\u0964 \u0905\u092a\u0928\u0947 \u0924\u092a\u094b\u092c\u0932 \u0914\u0930 \u0927\u0930\u094d\u092e \u0915\u0947 \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0924\u093f \u0905\u0938\u0940\u092e \u0938\u092e\u0930\u094d\u092a\u0923 \u0915\u0947 \u0915\u093e\u0930\u0923, \u092d\u0915\u094d\u0924\u0917\u0923 <strong>\u0907\u0928\u094d\u0939\u0947\u0902 \u0936\u0902\u0915\u0930\u093e\u091a\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f \u0915\u0947 \u0938\u092e\u0924\u0941\u0932\u094d\u092f \u0939\u0940 \u090f\u0915 \u092e\u0939\u093e\u0928 \u0935\u093f\u0926\u094d\u0935\u093e\u0928 \u0914\u0930 \u0924\u092a\u0938\u094d\u0935\u0940 \u092e\u093e\u0928\u0924\u0947 \u0939\u0948\u0902<\/strong> \u0914\u0930 \u0907\u0938\u0940 \u0936\u094d\u0930\u0926\u094d\u0927\u093e \u092d\u093e\u0935 \u0938\u0947 \u0907\u0928\u0915\u0940 \u092a\u0942\u091c\u093e-\u0905\u0930\u094d\u091a\u0928\u093e \u0915\u0930\u0924\u0947 \u0939\u0948\u0902\u0964<\/p>\n            <\/section>\n            <hr>\n            <!-- Part 1: Ancient Acharyas Table (1 to 67) -->\n            <section>\n                <h2>Part 1: Ancient Aacharyas (1st to 67th Aacharya)<\/h2>\n                <h2 style=\"display: none;\">\u092d\u093e\u0917 1: \u092a\u094d\u0930\u093e\u091a\u0940\u0928 \u0906\u091a\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f (\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0925\u092e \u0938\u0947 67\u0935\u0947\u0902 \u0906\u091a\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f \u0924\u0915)<\/h2>\n                    <table>\n                        <thead>\n                            <tr>\n                                <th>S.No.<\/th>\n                                <th>Name of the Aacharya<\/th>\n                                <th>Period (CE\/BCE)<\/th>\n                                <th>Key Details \/ Remarks<\/th>\n                            <\/tr>\n                            <tr style=\"display: none;\">\n                                <th>\u0915\u094d\u0930\u092e<\/th>\n                                <th>\u0906\u091a\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f \u0915\u093e \u0928\u093e\u092e<\/th>\n                                <th>\u0915\u093e\u0932-\u0916\u0902\u0921 (\u0908\u0938\u094d\u0935\u0940)<\/th>\n                                <th>\u092e\u0941\u0916\u094d\u092f \u0935\u093f\u0935\u0930\u0923 \/ \u091f\u093f\u092a\u094d\u092a\u0923\u0940<\/th>\n                            <\/tr>\n                        <\/thead>\n                        <!-- ENGLISH TABLE BODY -->\n                        <tbody>\n                            <tr><td>1.<\/td><td>Adi Shankaracharya<\/td><td>509 BCE \u2013 477 BCE<\/td><td>Founder of the Peetham and the First Aacharya.<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>2.<\/td><td>Sureshwaracharya<\/td><td>477 BCE \u2013 407 BCE<\/td><td>Prominent disciple of Adi Shankaracharya. Known as Mandana Mishra in earlier life.<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>3.<\/td><td>Sarvajnatman<\/td><td>407 BCE \u2013 364 BCE<\/td><td>Ascended the peetham as a Bala Brahmachari. Author of 'Sankshepa Sharirika'.<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>4.<\/td><td>Satyabodhendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>364 BCE \u2013 268 BCE<\/td><td>Resident of the Amravati region in Kerala.<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>5.<\/td><td>Jnananandendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>268 BCE \u2013 205 BCE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>6.<\/td><td>Shuddhanandendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>205 BCE \u2013 124 BCE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>7.<\/td><td>Anandaghanendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>124 BCE \u2013 55 BCE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>8.<\/td><td>Kaivalyananda Yogindra Saraswathi<\/td><td>55 BCE \u2013 28 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>9.<\/td><td>Krupashankarendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>28 CE \u2013 69 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>10.<\/td><td>Sureshwara Saraswathi<\/td><td>69 CE \u2013 127 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>11.<\/td><td>Shivananda Chidghanendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>127 CE \u2013 172 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>12.<\/td><td>Chandrashekarendra Saraswathi I<\/td><td>172 CE \u2013 235 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>13.<\/td><td>Sacchidghanendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>235 CE \u2013 273 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>14.<\/td><td>Vidyaghanendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>273 CE \u2013 317 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>15.<\/td><td>Gangadharendra Saraswathi I<\/td><td>317 CE \u2013 329 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>16.<\/td><td>Ujjvala Shankarendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>329 CE \u2013 367 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>17.<\/td><td>Sadashivendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>367 CE \u2013 375 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>18.<\/td><td>Shankarananda Saraswathi<\/td><td>375 CE \u2013 385 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>19.<\/td><td>Martanda Vidyaghanendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>385 CE \u2013 398 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>20.<\/td><td>Muka Shankarendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>398 CE \u2013 437 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>21.<\/td><td>Chandrashekarendra Saraswathi II<\/td><td>437 CE \u2013 447 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>22.<\/td><td>Bodhendra Saraswathi I<\/td><td>447 CE \u2013 481 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>23.<\/td><td>Sacchitsukhendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>481 CE \u2013 512 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>24.<\/td><td>Chitsukhendra Saraswathi I<\/td><td>512 CE \u2013 527 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>25.<\/td><td>Sacchidanandaghanendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>527 CE \u2013 548 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                            <tr><td>26.<\/td><td>Prajnaghanendra Saraswathi<\/td><td>548 CE \u2013 565 CE<\/td><td>-<\/td><\/tr>\n                       